  "scope": "Local macOS arm64 public SDK RTP/clock I/O, owned receive routing, bounded queues and SDK-published AV decoded at an independent canonical receiver. SDK reception is qualified by controlled signed negotiation and real QUIC datagrams. Authoritative Stream metadata, reliable data I/O, both-ends SDK decoded journeys, external crate, package, remote/Linux, performance and whole-task/acceptance qualification remain open.",
  "implementation": [
    "Scoped Stream handles bind full Conversation/Session/Connection/Stream identity and the exact native peer. Sending validates local ownership, direction and negotiated RTP payload type; saved or foreign-client handles cannot acquire hop handles.",
    "RtpPacket validates and preserves complete RTP bytes, including marker, CSRC, extensions, padding, timestamps, sequence and payload. The SDK supplies only the negotiated native handle and caller-owned independent datagram sequence.",
    "SenderClockReport remains distinct from RTP and requires negotiated rtcp-sr-sdes/1 support. Reports describe caller-provided source identity, counters and clock samples, never readiness or synchronized playback.",
    "One fair owned loop services reliable signaling/control and atomic media input/output. A 64-packet outgoing queue has bounded request deadline/cancellation. Successful sends prove local transport queue admission only; queued local cancellation/deadline can remain uncertain without a durable operation ID or automatic retry.",
    "Receive queues are shared by Stream clones, bounded to32packets per stream,256packets and4MiB per peer. Slow streams drain older packets then receive an explicit local Gap/drop count before new traffic resumes. Global counters distinguish malformed packets, foreign handles and local overflow. Read cancellation does not consume queued packets; close clears media and wakes readers.",
    "Client-side Stream snapshot decoding and distinct StreamResourceRevision are present, but the current Store deliberately never emits Stream snapshot rows. Stream.refresh remains unqualified and returns ReceiptUnavailable; no local-cache state is substituted for current server state."
  ],
